y record runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids February to March came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those 75 years. In 2025, July to August finished at 74% of normal and August to September at 63% on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, January to February sits at 47% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 22981 had its driest year in 1963 at 64% of normal.</p>"}
